# Ember

`ember-froala-editor` is an Ember addon with a `<FroalaEditor>` component, template helpers and test helpers. Its source is on [GitHub](https://github.com/froala/ember-froala-editor).

The addon's latest release, from November 2025, depends on `froala-editor ^4.7.1`, an older major version of the editor, so it installs that version, not the current one. For the current editor in Ember, install `froala-editor` and start it yourself with `new FroalaEditor(element, options)`, as the [Installation guide](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/overview/) shows.

## Compatibility

| Needs | Version |
| --- | --- |
| Ember.js | 3.20 or later |
| Ember CLI | 3.20 or later |
| Node.js | 18 or later |
| `ember-auto-import` | 2 or later |

## Installation

```shell
ember install ember-froala-editor
```

The addon brings in the editor's files. Your license key goes in `config/environment.js`, where every `<FroalaEditor>` reads its default options.

```js
// config/environment.js
let ENV = {
  'ember-froala-editor': {
    key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY'
  }
};
```

## Configuration

To add languages, plugins and themes to the build, list them in `ember-cli-build.js`. Each value is an array, as strings and booleans are no longer accepted. A plugin is named as in the [plugin list](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/plugins/) or by its file name without the extension.

```js
// ember-cli-build.js
let app = new EmberApp(defaults, {
  'ember-froala-editor': {
    languages: ['es', 'fr', 'de'],
    plugins: ['align', 'charCounter', 'paragraph_format'],
    themes: ['royal']
  }
});
```

## Usage

Pass the content as a SafeString from `htmlSafe` in `@content`, and a setter in `@update`, which gets the new content as a SafeString. Options go in `@options` or one by one as arguments.

```js
// app/components/post-editor.js
import Component from '@glimmer/component';
import { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking';
import { htmlSafe } from '@ember/template';

export default class PostEditor extends Component {
  @tracked content = htmlSafe('<p>Hello from Froala</p>');
}
```

```html
{{! app/components/post-editor.hbs }}
<FroalaEditor
  @content={{this.content}}
  @update={{fn (mut this.content)}}
  @placeholderText="Start writing"
/>
```

| Argument | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `@content` | The content, as a SafeString. |
| `@update` | Called with the new content, on `contentChanged` by default. |
| `@updateEvent` | The event that calls `@update`, such as `input`. |
| `@options` | The editor's [options](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/options/). An option passed as its own argument wins. |
| `@disabled` | Turns editing off and on, like `disabled` on a textarea. |
| `@on-*` | An event handler. See below. |

### Events

Prefix the [event](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/events/) name with `@on-`, and write a dot as a dash. The handler gets the editor as its first argument, then the event's own arguments.

```html
<FroalaEditor
  @on-focus={{this.onFocus}}
  @on-paste-afterCleanup={{this.onPaste}}
/>
```

```js
onFocus(editor) {
  console.log(editor.selection.get());
}

onPaste(editor, clipboardHtml) {
  return clipboardHtml;
}
```

### Displaying HTML

`<FroalaContent>` shows saved content in a `div` with the `fr-view` class. Its content is a SafeString too, so clean content from users you don't trust first.

```html
<FroalaContent @content={{this.content}} />
```

### Helpers

| Helper | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `froala-arg` | Passes the editor to a callback as its first argument, for handlers in the `events` option. |
| `froala-html` | Passes the editor's HTML to a callback as its first argument. |
| `froala-method` | Calls an editor [method](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/methods/) in place of a handler, such as `(froala-method "commands.undo")`. |
| `html-safe` | Turns a string into a SafeString for `@content`. |
| `to-string` | Turns the SafeString from `@update` back into a string. |
| `merged-hash` | Merges option objects, the last one winning. |

The last three aren't added to your app on their own. Generate a helper with the same name and re-export the addon's.

```shell
ember generate helper html-safe
```

```js
// app/helpers/html-safe.js
export { default } from 'ember-froala-editor/helpers/html-safe';
```

## Custom Buttons

Define buttons, dropdowns and icons once, in an application initializer, then name them in `toolbarButtons`.

```js
// app/initializers/froala-editor-elements.js
import FroalaEditor from 'froala-editor';

export function initialize() {
  FroalaEditor.DefineIcon('clear', { NAME: 'remove', SVG_KEY: 'remove' });
  FroalaEditor.RegisterCommand('clear', {
    title: 'Clear HTML',
    callback: function () {
      this.html.set('');
    }
  });
}

export default { initialize };
```

[Custom Button](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/concepts/custom/button/)

## Test Helpers

`fillInFroalaEditor` changes the editor's content in a test, as Ember's [`fillIn`](https://github.com/emberjs/ember-test-helpers/blob/master/API.md#fillin) does for a field. `getInFroalaEditor` returns the editor's HTML as a string.

```js
import { fillInFroalaEditor, getInFroalaEditor } from 'ember-froala-editor/test-support';

await fillInFroalaEditor('#editor', '<p>Foobaz</p>');
assert.strictEqual(getInFroalaEditor('#editor'), '<p>Foobaz</p>');
```

