# Vue

`vue-froala-wysiwyg` renders the editor as a Vue component. It works with Vue 3.2 and later, and its source is on [GitHub](https://github.com/froala/vue-froala-wysiwyg/).

## Installation

```shell
npm install froala-editor vue-froala-wysiwyg
```

The wrapper depends on the exact `froala-editor` version it was released with, so keep the two at the same version. To update, install both again with `@latest`.

```shell
npm install froala-editor@latest vue-froala-wysiwyg@latest
```

## Register the Component

### main.js

`app.use(VueFroala)` registers two components for the whole app, `froala` and `froala-view`. Import the editor's styles and the plugins you want in the same file.

```js
import { createApp } from 'vue';
import VueFroala from 'vue-froala-wysiwyg';
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins.pkgd.min.js';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_style.min.css';
import App from './App.vue';

const app = createApp(App);
app.use(VueFroala);
app.mount('#app');
```

### App.vue

```vue
<template>
  <froala :tag="'textarea'" :config="config" v-model:value="model" />
</template>

<script setup>
import { ref } from 'vue';

const config = {
  placeholderText: 'Edit your content here',
  charCounterCount: false
};
const model = ref('<p>Hello from Froala</p>');
</script>
```

Vite loads the CSS imports with no extra setup.

[How to integrate Froala with Vue 3](https://froala.com/blog/editor/tutorials/how-to-integrate-froala-with-vue-3/)

## Usage

| Prop | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `tag` | The element the editor starts on, `div` by default. `a`, `button`, `img` and `input` are [special tags](#special-tags). |
| `config` | The editor's options and events. |
| `v-model:value` | The content, as an HTML string, bound both ways. |
| `onManualControllerReady` | Lets you start the editor yourself. See [Manual Instantiation](#manual-instantiation). |

### Starting Content

Text inside the component is the editor's content until the model has a value, which replaces it.

```vue
<froala :tag="'textarea'" :config="config" v-model:value="model">Init text</froala>
```

### Options

`config` takes any of the editor's [options](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/options/). The component reads it once, when the editor starts, so later changes to the object don't reach it. Two more options belong to the wrapper.

| Option | Default | What it does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `immediateVueModelUpdate` | `false` | Updates the model each time a key is released, not only when the editor reports a change. It may slow typing. |
| `vueIgnoreAttrs` | `null` | For special tags, the attributes to leave out of the model. |

### Events and Methods

Put handlers in `config.events`, keyed by the [event](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/events/) name. Inside a handler, `this` is the editor, so write a regular function rather than an arrow function, and call any of the editor's [methods](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/methods/) on it.

```js
const config = {
  events: {
    initialized: function () {
      console.log('Ready with', this.html.get());
    },
    focus: function () {
      console.log(this.selection.get());
    }
  }
};
```

### Model

`v-model:value` keeps your ref and the editor in step. When the ref changes from outside, the editor replaces its content and starts a new undo history. Use the same ref anywhere else in the template.

```vue
<froala v-model:value="model" />
<textarea v-model="model"></textarea>
```

## Special Tags

On `img`, `button`, `input` and `a`, the model is an object of the element's attributes, and it follows the attributes as the user edits them. An `innerHTML` key sets what is inside the element, such as a button's label.

```vue
<template>
  <froala :tag="'img'" :config="config" v-model:value="image" />
  <froala :tag="'button'" :config="config" v-model:value="button" />
</template>

<script setup>
import { ref } from 'vue';

const config = { vueIgnoreAttrs: ['class', 'id'] };
const image = ref({ src: 'path/to/image.jpg' });
const button = ref({ innerHTML: 'Click me' });
</script>
```

### Ignored Attributes

`vueIgnoreAttrs` lists the attributes to leave out of the model, `null` by default.

[Special tags in a Vue app](https://froala.com/blog/editor/tutorials/web-editing-with-froalas-special-tags-in-vue-app/)

## Custom Buttons

Define each button's icon and command before the editor starts, then name the commands in `toolbarButtons`. Each inner list is a group of buttons.

```vue
<template>
  <froala :config="config" v-model:value="model" />
</template>

<script setup>
import { ref } from 'vue';
import FroalaEditor from 'froala-editor';

FroalaEditor.DefineIcon('clear', { NAME: 'remove', SVG_KEY: 'remove' });
FroalaEditor.RegisterCommand('clear', {
  title: 'Clear HTML',
  focus: false,
  undo: true,
  refreshAfterCallback: true,
  callback: function () {
    this.html.set('');
    this.events.focus();
  }
});

FroalaEditor.DefineIcon('insert', { NAME: 'plus', SVG_KEY: 'add' });
FroalaEditor.RegisterCommand('insert', {
  title: 'Insert HTML',
  focus: true,
  undo: true,
  refreshAfterCallback: true,
  callback: function () {
    this.html.insert('My New HTML');
  }
});

const config = {
  toolbarButtons: [['undo', 'redo'], ['bold'], ['clear', 'insert']]
};
const model = ref('');
</script>
```

- [Custom Button](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/concepts/custom/button/)
- [Custom buttons in Vue](https://froala.com/blog/editor/tutorials/vuejs-froala-custom-buttons/)

## Manual Instantiation

With `onManualControllerReady`, the component doesn't start the editor. It calls your function once, when it mounts, with an object of three methods.

| Method | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `initialize` | Starts the editor. |
| `destroy` | Destroys the editor. |
| `getEditor` | Returns the editor, or `null` before it starts. |

```vue
<template>
  <button @click="controls.initialize()">Edit</button>
  <button @click="clear">Clear</button>
  <froala :onManualControllerReady="onReady" v-model:value="model" />
</template>

<script setup>
import { ref, shallowRef } from 'vue';

const model = ref('<p>Click Edit to start.</p>');
const controls = shallowRef(null);

function onReady(c) {
  controls.value = c;
}

function clear() {
  const editor = controls.value.getEditor();
  editor.html.set('');
  editor.undo.reset();
  editor.undo.saveStep();
}
</script>
```

[Start the editor on click](https://froala.com/blog/editor/tutorials/optimizing-vue-applications-initializing-froala-editor-on-click/)

## Displaying HTML

`froala-view` shows saved content with the editor's styles, in a `div` with the `fr-view` class, or the element its `tag` prop names. It only displays, so pass the content with `:value`.

```vue
<froala v-model:value="content" />
<froala-view :value="content" />
```

`froala-view` writes the HTML to `innerHTML` as it is. Clean content from users you don't trust before you show it.

