# Migrate from Aloha Editor

Aloha Editor makes elements of a page editable in place. This guide replaces it with Froala on the same elements and maps the calls you use to Froala's.

Aloha Editor is developed on GitHub, where its latest release, 2.1.21, is from October 2026. It loads with RequireJS and uses jQuery. Froala needs neither.

## Initialization

### Remove Aloha Editor

Remove Aloha's stylesheet, RequireJS, `aloha.js` with its plugin list, any jQuery you load only for Aloha, and the script that makes the elements editable. Settings in `Aloha.settings` go too.

```html
<!-- Remove -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/javascripts/aloha/css/aloha.css" type="text/css">
<script src="/javascripts/aloha/lib/require.js"></script>
<script src="/javascripts/aloha/lib/aloha.js"
  data-aloha-plugins="common/ui,common/format,common/highlighteditables,common/link"></script>
<script>
  Aloha.ready(function () {
    Aloha.jQuery('#content').aloha();
  });
</script>
```

### Add Froala

Add the editor's stylesheet in the `head` and its script at the end of the `body`. The editor draws its icons as SVG and needs neither Font Awesome nor jQuery.

```html
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/froala_editor.pkgd.min.js"></script>
```

With a bundler, install the package and import the same files.

```shell
npm install froala-editor
```

Start the editor on the element Aloha edited. The editor starts on any element, and a selector that matches several starts one editor on each. `toolbarInline` shows the toolbar next to the selected text, for editing in place.

```js
// Aloha Editor
Aloha.ready(function () {
  Aloha.jQuery('#content').aloha();
});

// Froala
var editor = new FroalaEditor('#content', {
  key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY',
  toolbarInline: true
});
```

### Full Example

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>Migrate from Aloha Editor to Froala</title>
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="main">
      <div id="content"><p>Getting started</p></div>
    </div>

    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/froala_editor.pkgd.min.js"></script>
    <script>
      var editor = new FroalaEditor('#content', {
        key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY',
        toolbarInline: true
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
```

[Activation](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/activation/)

## Map the API

Froala's methods belong to the editor that `new FroalaEditor()` returns. Inside an event handler, `this` is the editor, so write a regular function rather than an arrow function.

| Task | Aloha Editor | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Settings | `Aloha.settings`, set before `aloha.js` loads | The options object passed to `new FroalaEditor()` |
| Plugins | The `data-aloha-plugins` list on the script | The packaged script holds the plugins, and `pluginsEnabled` picks them |
| Make editable | `Aloha.jQuery('#content').aloha()` | `new FroalaEditor('#content')` |
| Stop editing | `Aloha.jQuery('#content').mahalo()` | `editor.destroy()`, or `editor.edit.off()` to keep the editor read-only |
| Read the HTML | `Aloha.getEditableById('content').getContents()` | `editor.html.get()` |
| Write the HTML | `Aloha.getEditableById('content').setContents(html)` | `editor.html.set(html)` |
| Content changed | `Aloha.bind('aloha-smart-content-changed', handler)` | The `contentChanged` event |
| Editing starts or ends | `aloha-editable-activated`, `aloha-editable-deactivated` | The `focus` and `blur` events |

```js
// Aloha Editor
Aloha.ready(function () {
  Aloha.jQuery('#content').aloha();
  Aloha.bind('aloha-smart-content-changed', function (jEvent, data) {
    console.log(Aloha.getEditableById('content').getContents());
  });
});

// Froala
var editor = new FroalaEditor('#content', {
  toolbarInline: true,
  events: {
    contentChanged: function () {
      console.log(this.html.get());
    }
  }
});
```

- [Options](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/options/)
- [Events](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/events/)
- [Methods](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/methods/)

## Match the Features

| Feature | In Froala |
| --- | --- |
| Editing in place | `toolbarInline: true`, and `toolbarVisibleWithoutSelection` to keep the toolbar next to the cursor |
| Images | The Image plugin. Set `imageUploadURL`, and your server returns JSON with a `link` field. Users can also drop or paste images, insert them by URL, resize them and add captions. |
| Custom formats | `inlineClasses` for selected text and `paragraphStyles` for paragraphs, each a class you define in your CSS with its label |

```js
new FroalaEditor('#content', {
  toolbarInline: true,
  imageUploadURL: '/upload_image',
  inlineClasses: { 'fr-class-highlighted': 'Highlighted', 'fr-class-code': 'Code' },
  paragraphStyles: { 'fr-text-bordered': 'Bordered' }
});
```

- [Feature matching](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/migration-guides/aloha/feature-matching/)
- [Image upload](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/concepts/image/upload/)

# Migrate Aloha Options to Froala Editor

## Options

The following guide explains how to pass different Froala Editor options and highlights what to do when migrating from other WYSIWYG editors.



### 1\. Running the code

Aloha and Froala use a DOM selector to fetch the element that includes the editor. The following example uses a div tag that has its id value set to ‘editor’ to get the containing element.

Aloha WYSIWYG Editor

```
<script type="text/javascript">
  Aloha.ready(function(){
    Aloha.jQuery('#editor').aloha();
  });
</script>
```

Froala Editor.

```
<script>
  var editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor');
</script>
```

Froala Editor can initialize on more elements than other editors:

-   You can initiate Froala on an image using the image.min.js plugin

```
<!-- HTML -->
<img id="edit" src=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/froala/wysiwyg-editor/master/editor.jpg" alt="Old Clock" width="300"/>

<!-- Javascript  -->
<script>
  new FroalaEditor('#img#edit');
</script>
```

-   It is possible to initialize the Froala Editor only on a button

```
<!-- HTML -->
<button id="edit" class="btn r-btn highlight text-small">Button</button>

<!-- Javascript  -->
<script>
  new FroalaEditor('button#edit');
</script>
```

-   It is possible to initialize the Froala Editor on click on an element

```
<!-- HTML -->
<div id="editor">Hello ContentTools</div>

<!-- Javascript  -->
<script>
  new FroalaEditor('#editor',{
    initOnClick: true
  });
</script>
```

### 2\. Working with plugins

Froala Editor comes with over 30 plugins. You can enable the plugins you want to use at initialization.

**Note:** By default, all plugins are enabled without using the pluginsEnabled option. Also, each plugin requires you to include the corresponding JS and CSS files. Here is the [complete list of plugins](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/plugins/) and the files required by them.

Aloha WYSIWYG Editor

```
Aloha.settings = {
  plugins:{
    format:{
      // all elements with no specific configuration get this configuration
      config:['b', 'i', 'sub', 'sup', 'p', 'h1', 'h2', 'h3', 'h4', 'h5', 'h6'],
      editables:{
        // no formatting allowed for title
        '#title': [],
        // just bold and italic for the teaser
        '#teaser': ['b', 'i']
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Froala Editor

```
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  pluginsEnabled: ['image', 'link']
});
```

If you don’t find the plugin you want, you can create your own.

### 3\. Toolbar Customizations

Aloha and Froala Editors allow the customization of the toolbar. In Froala Editor you can choose how to group buttons and also set them to adapt based on the screen size, this allows the editor to display properly on all devices. For a complete list of options please refer to the [Options](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/options/) documentation.

Aloha toolbar customizations

```
Aloha.settings.toolbar = {
  tabs: [
    {
      label: 'Format',
      components: [
        ['bold', 'italic', 'underline', '\n', 'subscript', 'superscript', 'strikethrough'],
        ['formatBlock']
      ]
    },
    {
      label: 'Insert',
      exclusive: true,
      components: [
        ["createTable", "characterPicker", "insertLink"],
        ['myArena']
      ]
    },
    {
      label: 'Link',
      components: ['editlink']
    }
  ],
  exclude:['strong', 'emphasis', 'strikethrough'],
  responsiveMode: false
};
```

Froala Editor

```
<script>
  new FroalaEditor('#editor',{
    pluginsEnabled:['image','link','Table'],
    toolbarButtons:[
      'undo','redo','|','bold','italic','|','insertLink','insertImage','-','alignLeft',
      'alignCenter','alignRight'
    ]
  });
</script>
```

