# Migrate from CKEditor

Replace CKEditor 5 with Froala in an existing project. Each section maps a CKEditor 5 concept to its Froala equivalent, with both in one code block.

Froala takes your license key as the `key` option. [Start a free trial](https://froala.com/wysiwyg_editor-download/) or [buy a license](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/pricing/) to get one. For help along the way, [contact support](https://froala.com/contact/?department=Tech%20Support).

## How the Editors Differ

In CKEditor 5 a feature exists once you import its plugin and list it. Froala's packaged file comes with its plugins loaded and on, so most of the work is translating configuration, not assembling features.

| Concept | CKEditor 5 | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Create the editor | `ClassicEditor.create({ attachTo, ...config })`, a Promise | `new FroalaEditor(selector, options, callback)` |
| Target | A DOM element | A CSS selector or a DOM element |
| Features | Import plugins and list them in `plugins` | Loaded with the packaged file; narrow them with `pluginsEnabled` |
| Toolbar | `toolbar` | `toolbarButtons` |
| Content | `getData()`, `setData()` | `html.get()`, `html.set()` |
| License | `licenseKey`, `'GPL'` or a commercial key | `key`, a commercial key |

## Replace CKEditor

### Remove CKEditor

#### With npm

Remove `ckeditor5`, and `ckeditor5-premium-features` and `@ckeditor/ckeditor5-react` if you use them. Older projects may use a predefined build such as `@ckeditor/ckeditor5-build-classic` instead.

```shell
npm uninstall ckeditor5 ckeditor5-premium-features @ckeditor/ckeditor5-react
```

#### With the CDN

```html
<!-- Remove these -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.ckeditor.com/ckeditor5/49.0.1/ckeditor5.css">
<script src="https://cdn.ckeditor.com/ckeditor5/49.0.1/ckeditor5.umd.js"></script>
```

Remove the `ClassicEditor.create()` call too. You replace it in the next step.

### Add Froala

#### With the CDN

The packaged files hold the editor and every plugin except Track Changes and Trim Video, the closest match to a full CKEditor 5 setup.

```html
<!-- In the head -->
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css" rel="stylesheet">

<!-- Before the closing body tag -->
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/froala_editor.pkgd.min.js"></script>
```

#### With npm

```shell
npm install froala-editor
```

```js
import FroalaEditor from 'froala-editor';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css';

// Every plugin
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins.pkgd.min.js';

// Or only the plugins you need
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins/align.min.js';
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins/lists.min.js';
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins/image.min.js';
```

### Start the Editor

CKEditor 5 resolves a Promise with the editor. Froala's constructor returns the editor at once and takes a function as its third argument, which runs when the editor is ready, as `.then()` does.

```js
// CKEditor 5
import { ClassicEditor, Essentials, Bold, Italic, Paragraph } from 'ckeditor5';
import 'ckeditor5/ckeditor5.css';

ClassicEditor
  .create({
    attachTo: document.querySelector('#editor'),
    licenseKey: 'GPL',
    plugins: [Essentials, Bold, Italic, Paragraph],
    toolbar: ['undo', 'redo', '|', 'bold', 'italic']
  })
  .then(editor => console.log('Ready', editor))
  .catch(err => console.error(err));

// Froala
const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY',
  toolbarButtons: [['undo', 'redo'], ['bold', 'italic']]
}, function () {
  console.log('Ready', this);
});
```

Call the editor's methods, such as `editor.html.get()`, from that function, the `initialized` event or later. Right after the constructor they don't exist yet.

Older CKEditor code passes the element first, as `ClassicEditor.create(element, config)`. It maps to Froala the same way.

### A Complete Page

```html
<!doctype html>
<html>
  <head>
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="editor"><p>Hello world</p></div>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/froala_editor.pkgd.min.js"></script>
    <script>
      new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
        key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY',
        toolbarButtons: [['bold', 'italic', 'underline'], ['insertLink']]
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
```

## Configuration and Options

### Toolbar

Both editors take an ordered list of named buttons. In Froala each inner array is a group; a flat list split with `'|'` works too. Most of the migration is renaming the buttons.

| Action | CKEditor 5 item | Froala button |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bold, italic, underline | `bold`, `italic`, `underline` | The same names |
| Headings | `heading` | `paragraphFormat` |
| Lists | `bulletedList`, `numberedList` | `formatUL`, `formatOL` |
| Link | `link` | `insertLink` |
| Image | `uploadImage`, `insertImage` | `insertImage` |
| Table | `insertTable` | `insertTable` |
| Block quote | `blockQuote` | `quote` |
| Alignment | `alignment` | `align`, or `alignLeft`, `alignCenter`, `alignRight` |
| Font color | `fontColor` | `textColor` |
| Remove formatting | `removeFormat` | `clearFormatting` |
| Undo, redo | `undo`, `redo` | `undo`, `redo` |

```js
// CKEditor 5
toolbar: ['heading', '|', 'bold', 'italic', 'link', '|', 'bulletedList', 'numberedList', 'insertTable']

// Froala
toolbarButtons: [
  ['paragraphFormat'],
  ['bold', 'italic'],
  ['insertLink', 'insertTable'],
  ['formatUL', 'formatOL']
]
```

For smaller screens, Froala takes separate lists in `toolbarButtonsMD`, `toolbarButtonsSM` and `toolbarButtonsXS`.

### Common Options

| CKEditor 5 | Froala |
| --- | --- |
| `licenseKey` | `key` |
| `root.placeholder`, or `placeholder` in older code | `placeholderText` |
| `language` with `translations` | `language` with its file from `froala-editor/js/languages/` |
| `root.initialData`, or `initialData` in older code | The element's HTML, or `html.set()` once ready |

```js
// CKEditor 5
import translations from 'ckeditor5/translations/fr.js';

ClassicEditor.create({
  attachTo: document.querySelector('#editor'),
  licenseKey: 'GPL',
  language: 'fr',
  translations: [translations],
  root: {
    placeholder: 'Write something',
    initialData: '<p>Welcome</p>'
  }
});

// Froala
import 'froala-editor/js/languages/fr.js';

new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY',
  language: 'fr',
  placeholderText: 'Write something'
}, function () {
  this.html.set('<p>Welcome</p>');
});
```

## Plugins

With the packaged file, every Froala plugin is loaded and on. `pluginsEnabled` keeps only the plugins it names, and `pluginsDisabled` turns off the ones it names.

```js
// CKEditor 5
import { ClassicEditor, Essentials, Bold, Italic, Link, List, Image, Table, Paragraph } from 'ckeditor5';

ClassicEditor.create({
  attachTo: document.querySelector('#editor'),
  licenseKey: 'GPL',
  plugins: [Essentials, Bold, Italic, Link, List, Image, Table, Paragraph]
});

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  pluginsEnabled: ['link', 'lists', 'image', 'table'],
  toolbarButtons: [['bold', 'italic'], ['insertLink', 'insertImage', 'insertTable'], ['formatUL']]
});
```

[Plugins](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/plugins/)

## Getting and Setting Content

```js
// CKEditor 5
const html = editor.getData();
editor.setData('<p>New content</p>');

// Froala
const html = editor.html.get();
editor.html.set('<p>New content</p>');

// Insert at the cursor
editor.html.insert('<strong>Inserted</strong>');
```

To show saved content outside the editor with its formatting, put it in an element with the `fr-view` class and load `froala_style.min.css`.

## Events

CKEditor 5 fires events on several objects, the model document for changes and the view document for focus. Froala takes every handler in one `events` object. Inside a handler, `this` is the editor, so write regular functions rather than arrow functions.

```js
// CKEditor 5
ClassicEditor
  .create({ attachTo: document.querySelector('#editor'), licenseKey: 'GPL' })
  .then(editor => {
    editor.model.document.on('change:data', () => console.log(editor.getData()));
    editor.editing.view.document.on('focus', () => console.log('Focused'));
    editor.editing.view.document.on('blur', () => console.log('Blurred'));
  });

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  events: {
    initialized: function () { console.log('Ready'); },
    contentChanged: function () { console.log(this.html.get()); },
    focus: function () { console.log('Focused'); },
    blur: function () { console.log('Blurred'); }
  }
});
```

[Events](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/events/)

## Methods

### Read-Only Mode

CKEditor 5 locks read-only mode with an id. Froala turns editing off and on directly.

```js
// CKEditor 5
editor.enableReadOnlyMode('my-lock');
editor.disableReadOnlyMode('my-lock');

// Froala
editor.edit.off();
editor.edit.on();
```

### Focus and Destroy

CKEditor 5 destroys the editor with a Promise. Froala's `destroy()` returns at once and puts the element back as it was.

```js
// CKEditor 5
editor.focus();
editor.destroy().then(() => console.log('Destroyed'));

// Froala
editor.events.focus();
editor.destroy();
```

[Methods](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/methods/)

## Image Upload

CKEditor 5 uploads through an adapter plugin, such as `SimpleUploadAdapter`. Froala's Image plugin sends each image to `imageUploadURL` as a `POST` form, in the field `imageUploadParam` names (`file` by default), with the headers in `requestHeaders`.

```js
// CKEditor 5
import { ClassicEditor, Essentials, Paragraph, Image, ImageUpload, SimpleUploadAdapter } from 'ckeditor5';

ClassicEditor.create({
  attachTo: document.querySelector('#editor'),
  licenseKey: 'GPL',
  plugins: [Essentials, Paragraph, Image, ImageUpload, SimpleUploadAdapter],
  simpleUpload: {
    uploadUrl: '/upload',
    headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer <token>' }
  }
});

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  imageUploadURL: '/upload',
  requestHeaders: { Authorization: 'Bearer <token>' },
  imageMaxSize: 5 * 1024 * 1024,
  imageAllowedTypes: ['jpeg', 'jpg', 'png', 'gif'],
  events: {
    'image.error': function (error, response) {
      console.error(error.code, error.message);
    }
  }
});
```

Change what your server returns. Simple Upload reads `{ "url": "/path/to/image.jpg" }`; Froala reads `{ "link": "/path/to/image.jpg" }`.

[Image upload](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/concepts/image/upload/)

## React

`react-froala-wysiwyg` takes the options in `config`, the content in `model`, and calls `onModelChange` with the new HTML, where the CKEditor component calls `onChange` with the editor.

```shell
npm uninstall @ckeditor/ckeditor5-react ckeditor5
npm install froala-editor react-froala-wysiwyg
```

```jsx
// CKEditor 5
import { CKEditor } from '@ckeditor/ckeditor5-react';
import { ClassicEditor, Essentials, Bold, Italic, Paragraph } from 'ckeditor5';
import 'ckeditor5/ckeditor5.css';

export function MyEditor() {
  return (
    <CKEditor
      editor={ClassicEditor}
      config={{ licenseKey: 'GPL', plugins: [Essentials, Bold, Italic, Paragraph], toolbar: ['bold', 'italic'] }}
      data="<p>Hello world</p>"
      onChange={(event, editor) => console.log(editor.getData())}
    />
  );
}

// Froala
import { useState } from 'react';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_style.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins.pkgd.min.js';
import FroalaEditorComponent from 'react-froala-wysiwyg';

const config = { key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY', toolbarButtons: [['bold', 'italic']] };

export function MyEditor() {
  const [model, setModel] = useState('<p>Hello world</p>');

  return (
    <FroalaEditorComponent tag="textarea" config={config} model={model} onModelChange={setModel} />
  );
}
```

[React guide](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/framework-plugins/react/)

## Lookup Table

| To | CKEditor 5 | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Create | `ClassicEditor.create({ attachTo, ...config })` | `new FroalaEditor(selector, options, callback)` |
| Run code when ready | `.then(editor => {})` | The callback, or the `initialized` event |
| Get HTML | `editor.getData()` | `editor.html.get()` |
| Set HTML | `editor.setData(html)` | `editor.html.set(html)` |
| Insert HTML | `editor.model.insertContent()` | `editor.html.insert(html)` |
| Toolbar | `toolbar` | `toolbarButtons` |
| Placeholder | `root.placeholder` | `placeholderText` |
| Language | `language` | `language` |
| Read-only on, off | `enableReadOnlyMode(id)`, `disableReadOnlyMode(id)` | `edit.off()`, `edit.on()` |
| Focus | `editor.focus()` | `editor.events.focus()` |
| Destroy | `editor.destroy()`, a Promise | `editor.destroy()` |
| Content changed | `model.document.on('change:data')` | The `contentChanged` event |
| Image upload URL | `simpleUpload.uploadUrl` | `imageUploadURL` |
| License | `licenseKey` | `key` |

