# Migrate from TinyMCE

Replace TinyMCE with Froala in an existing project. Each section maps a TinyMCE setting or call to its Froala equivalent, with both in one code block.

Froala takes your license key as the `key` option. [Start a free trial](https://froala.com/wysiwyg_editor-download/) or [buy a license](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/pricing/) to get one. For help along the way, [contact support](https://froala.com/contact/?department=Tech%20Support).

## Why Teams Switch

The two editors are licensed and billed differently.

| Topic | TinyMCE | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| License | Open source under GPL 2 or later when self-hosted, or a commercial plan | A commercial license per product and domain |
| Usage | Tiny Cloud plans include a monthly number of editor loads and charge for loads above it | Unlimited editor loads and active users on every plan, with no overage charges |

[Froala and TinyMCE compared](https://froala.com/blog/general/compare-froala-tinymce-the-best-wysiwyg-editor/)

## Replace TinyMCE

Take out the TinyMCE files, then add Froala's. The packaged files hold the editor and its plugins.

### From Tiny Cloud

```html
<!-- Remove TinyMCE -->
<script src="https://cdn.tiny.cloud/1/YOUR_API_KEY/tinymce/8/tinymce.min.js" referrerpolicy="origin"></script>

<!-- Add Froala, the stylesheet in the head and the script before the closing body tag -->
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/froala_editor.pkgd.min.js"></script>
```

### From Self-Hosted TinyMCE

Point the tags at your own copy of the `froala-editor` package.

```html
<!-- Remove TinyMCE -->
<script src="/path/to/tinymce/tinymce.min.js"></script>

<!-- Add Froala -->
<link href="/path/to/froala-editor/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
<script src="/path/to/froala-editor/js/froala_editor.pkgd.min.js"></script>
```

### From npm

Remove `tinymce` and any wrapper you use, such as `@tinymce/tinymce-react`, then install Froala.

```shell
npm uninstall tinymce @tinymce/tinymce-react
npm install froala-editor
```

```js
import FroalaEditor from 'froala-editor';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins.pkgd.min.js';
```

[Installation](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/overview/)

## Start the Editor

`new FroalaEditor()` takes a CSS selector or an element, your options, and an optional function that runs once the editor is ready. It starts on a `div` or a `textarea`, and what the element holds becomes the starting content.

```html
<!-- TinyMCE -->
<textarea id="editor">Hello, World!</textarea>
<script>
  tinymce.init({ selector: '#editor' });
</script>

<!-- Froala -->
<div id="editor">Hello, World!</div>
<script>
  const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', { key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY' }, function () {
    console.log(this.html.get());
  });
</script>
```

The constructor returns the editor at once, but its methods, such as `editor.html`, are ready only when that function runs or the `initialized` event fires. Call them from there or later.

## Configuration Options

Most TinyMCE settings have a Froala option of a similar name.

| TinyMCE | Froala | Note |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `selector` | First argument of `new FroalaEditor()` | A selector or an element |
| `toolbar` | `toolbarButtons` | An array of button groups |
| `placeholder` | `placeholderText` |  |
| `readonly` | `edit.off()` | A method, called once the editor is ready |
| `height`, `width` | `height`, `width` | Also `heightMin` and `heightMax` |
| `content_css` | `iframeStyleFiles` | With `iframe: true` |
| `content_style` | `iframeStyle` | With `iframe: true` |
| `plugins` | `pluginsEnabled`, `pluginsDisabled` | See [Plugins](#plugins) |
| `language` | `language` | Load the language file too |
| `license_key` or the Cloud API key | `key` |  |
| `images_upload_url` | `imageUploadURL` | See [Image Upload](#image-upload) |
| `setup` with `editor.on()` | `events` | See [Events](#events) |

### Toolbar

TinyMCE separates groups with `|` in a string. Froala takes an array, each inner array a group of buttons. For smaller screens, set `toolbarButtonsMD`, `toolbarButtonsSM` and `toolbarButtonsXS`.

```js
// TinyMCE
tinymce.init({
  selector: '#editor',
  toolbar: 'undo redo | bold italic underline | alignleft aligncenter alignright | bullist numlist'
});

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  toolbarButtons: [
    ['undo', 'redo'],
    ['bold', 'italic', 'underline'],
    ['alignLeft', 'alignCenter', 'alignRight', 'formatUL', 'formatOL']
  ]
});
```

| TinyMCE button | Froala button |
| --- | --- |
| `bold`, `italic`, `underline`, `undo`, `redo`, `fullscreen` | The same names |
| `alignleft`, `aligncenter`, `alignright`, `alignjustify` | `alignLeft`, `alignCenter`, `alignRight`, `alignJustify` |
| `bullist`, `numlist` | `formatUL`, `formatOL` |
| `blocks` | `paragraphFormat` |
| `fontfamily`, `fontsize` | `fontFamily`, `fontSize` |
| `forecolor`, `backcolor` | `textColor`, `backgroundColor` |
| `removeformat` | `clearFormatting` |
| `blockquote` | `quote` |
| `link`, `image`, `media`, `table` | `insertLink`, `insertImage`, `insertVideo`, `insertTable` |
| `hr`, `charmap`, `emoticons` | `insertHR`, `specialCharacters`, `emoticons` |
| `code` | `html` |

### Placeholder Text

```js
// TinyMCE
tinymce.init({ selector: '#editor', placeholder: 'Start typing here' });

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', { placeholderText: 'Start typing here' });
```

### Read-Only Mode

Froala has no read-only option. Turn editing off with `edit.off()` once the editor is ready, and back on with `edit.on()`.

```js
// TinyMCE
tinymce.init({ selector: '#editor', readonly: true });

// Later, to edit again
tinymce.get('editor').mode.set('design');

// Froala
const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  events: {
    initialized: function () {
      this.edit.off();
    }
  }
});

// Later, to edit again
editor.edit.on();
```

### Height and Width

```js
// TinyMCE
tinymce.init({ selector: '#editor', height: 400, width: 800 });

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', { height: 400, width: 800 });
```

### Content Styling

TinyMCE edits in an iframe and styles it with `content_css`. Froala edits in your page by default, so your stylesheet already reaches the content; `editorClass` adds a class to the editor's box to scope it. To edit in an iframe as TinyMCE does, set `iframe: true` and pass your stylesheet in `iframeStyleFiles`, or CSS text in `iframeStyle`.

```js
// TinyMCE
tinymce.init({
  selector: '#editor',
  content_css: '/path/to/custom-content.css'
});

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  iframe: true,
  iframeStyleFiles: ['/path/to/custom-content.css']
});
```

## Plugins

TinyMCE turns on the plugins you list. Froala's packaged file, `froala_editor.pkgd.min.js`, already holds every plugin except Track Changes and Trim Video, and all of them are on. `pluginsEnabled` keeps only the ones it names, and `pluginsDisabled` turns off the ones it names.

```js
// TinyMCE
tinymce.init({
  selector: '#editor',
  plugins: 'lists link image table code'
});

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  pluginsEnabled: ['lists', 'link', 'image', 'table', 'codeView']
});
```

To load fewer files, use the core editor and add each plugin's script, and its stylesheet where it has one.

```html
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/css/froala_editor.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/css/plugins/table.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/froala_editor.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/plugins/lists.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/plugins/link.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/plugins/table.min.js"></script>
```

| TinyMCE plugin | Froala plugin |
| --- | --- |
| `lists`, `link`, `image`, `table`, `fullscreen`, `emoticons` | The same names |
| `code` | `codeView` |
| `media` | `video` |
| `charmap` | `specialCharacters` |
| `searchreplace` | `findReplace` |
| `wordcount` | `wordCounter`, `charCounter` |

[Plugins](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/plugins/)

## Events

TinyMCE binds events in `setup`. Froala takes an `events` object in its options. Inside a handler, `this` is the editor, so write regular functions rather than arrow functions.

| TinyMCE event | Froala event |
| --- | --- |
| `init` | `initialized` |
| `change` | `contentChanged` |
| `focus`, `blur`, `input`, `keydown`, `keyup` | The same names |

```js
// TinyMCE
tinymce.init({
  selector: '#editor',
  setup: function (editor) {
    editor.on('init', function () { console.log('Ready'); });
    editor.on('change', function () { console.log(editor.getContent()); });
    editor.on('focus', function () { console.log('Focused'); });
    editor.on('blur', function () { console.log('Blurred'); });
  }
});

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  events: {
    initialized: function () { console.log('Ready'); },
    contentChanged: function () { console.log(this.html.get()); },
    focus: function () { console.log('Focused'); },
    blur: function () { console.log('Blurred'); }
  }
});
```

To bind a handler later, call `editor.events.on('contentChanged', handler)` once the editor is ready.

## Methods

TinyMCE looks an editor up with `tinymce.get(id)`. With Froala, keep the instance that `new FroalaEditor()` returns, or use `this` inside a handler.

| To | TinyMCE | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Get the content | `getContent()` | `html.get()` |
| Set the content | `setContent(html)` | `html.set(html)` |
| Insert at the cursor | `insertContent(html)` | `html.insert(html)` |
| Focus | `focus()` | `events.focus()` |
| Undo, redo | `execCommand('undo')`, `execCommand('redo')` | `commands.undo()`, `commands.redo()` |
| Read-only on, off | `mode.set('readonly')`, `mode.set('design')` | `edit.off()`, `edit.on()` |
| Destroy | `remove()` | `destroy()` |

```js
// TinyMCE
const content = tinymce.get('editor').getContent();
tinymce.get('editor').setContent('<p>New content</p>');
tinymce.get('editor').insertContent('<strong>Inserted text</strong>');
tinymce.get('editor').remove();

// Froala
const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', {}, function () {
  const content = editor.html.get();
  editor.html.set('<p>New content</p>');
  editor.html.insert('<strong>Inserted text</strong>');
  editor.events.focus();
  editor.commands.undo();
});

// Later, to remove the editor and start a new one on the same element
editor.destroy();
const next = new FroalaEditor('#editor', {});
```

Froala has no blur method. To move focus out, call `editor.el.blur()`, where `editor.el` is the editable element.

[Methods](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/methods/)

## Image Upload

Froala builds the upload request itself. It sends each image to `imageUploadURL` as a `POST` form, in the field `imageUploadParam` names (`file` by default), with any extra fields from `imageUploadParams`. There is no handler to write.

```js
// TinyMCE
tinymce.init({
  selector: '#editor',
  plugins: 'image',
  images_upload_url: '/api/upload-image',
  // Or your own handler, which returns a Promise of the image URL
  images_upload_handler: (blobInfo, progress) => {
    const body = new FormData();
    body.append('file', blobInfo.blob(), blobInfo.filename());
    return fetch('/api/upload-image', { method: 'POST', body })
      .then(res => res.json())
      .then(json => json.location);
  }
});

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  imageUploadURL: '/api/upload-image',
  imageUploadParam: 'file',
  imageUploadParams: { folder: 'posts' },
  events: {
    'image.uploaded': function (response) {
      console.log('Uploaded', response);
    },
    'image.error': function (error, response) {
      console.error(error.code, error.message);
    }
  }
});
```

Change what your server returns. TinyMCE reads `{ "location": "/path/to/image.jpg" }`; Froala reads `{ "link": "/path/to/image.jpg" }`.

[Image upload](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/concepts/image/upload/)

