# Migrate from Lexical

Move an editor from Lexical to Froala. Each section pairs a Lexical call with its Froala counterpart, checked against Lexical 0.53.0, the current release.

## Before You Start

Lexical is an editor framework. It attaches to a contenteditable element and keeps its own model of the document, the editor state. You compose its features from optional packages and build the toolbar yourself.

Froala is a complete editor. One call gives you the toolbar and the plugins, and the content is HTML, read with `html.get()` and written with `html.set()`.

| Concept | Lexical | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Start | `createEditor(config)`, then `setRootElement(element)` | `new FroalaEditor('#editor', options)` |
| Features | Packages, their nodes and their `register` calls | Plugins, all on once loaded |
| Toolbar | Your own, dispatching commands such as `FORMAT_TEXT_COMMAND` | `toolbarButtons` |
| Content | The editor state, a node tree | HTML, `html.get()` and `html.set()` |
| Events | `registerUpdateListener(listener)` | The `events` option, or `events.on()` |
| Tear down | `setRootElement(null)`, then each cleanup function | `destroy()` |
| License | MIT, free | Commercial, a license key in the `key` option |

Without a valid key, Froala shows a small notice, and every feature keeps working. Use the key from your [license](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/pricing/) or a [free trial](https://froala.com/wysiwyg_editor-download/).

## Replace Lexical

### Remove Lexical

Remove the Lexical packages you installed, then the setup code, the `createEditor` call, `setRootElement` and the `register` calls, or the `LexicalComposer` tree in React.

```shell
npm uninstall lexical @lexical/react @lexical/rich-text @lexical/html @lexical/list @lexical/link @lexical/history
```

### Add Froala

```html
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/froala_editor.pkgd.min.js"></script>
```

Or install it with npm and import it.

```shell
npm install froala-editor
```

```js
import FroalaEditor from 'froala-editor';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins.pkgd.min.js';
```

The packaged files hold every plugin except Track Changes and Trim Video.

[Installation](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/overview/)

### Start the Editor

One constructor replaces the engine setup. It takes a selector or an element, a `div` or a `textarea` for example, and starts with the element's HTML as its content.

```js
// Lexical
import { createEditor } from 'lexical';
import { registerRichText } from '@lexical/rich-text';

const editor = createEditor({ namespace: 'MyEditor', onError: console.error });
editor.setRootElement(document.getElementById('editor'));
registerRichText(editor);

// Froala
import FroalaEditor from 'froala-editor';

const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', { key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY' });
```

## Configuration and Options

Lexical's `createEditor` config holds the namespace, theme classes, nodes and error handler, and the behavior lives in the packages you register. Froala's options object holds everything, from size and placeholder to toolbar and counters.

| Lexical | Froala |
| --- | --- |
| `namespace` | Not needed; each editor is separate |
| `theme`, class names for nodes | Plain HTML tags, styled with CSS; `editorClass` adds a class to the editing area |
| `nodes` | The plugins you load |
| `editable: false` | `this.edit.off()` in the `initialized` event |

```js
// Lexical
const editor = createEditor({
  namespace: 'MyEditor',
  theme: { paragraph: 'my-paragraph', text: { bold: 'my-bold' } },
  nodes: [HeadingNode, ListNode, ListItemNode, LinkNode],
  onError: (error) => console.error(error)
});

// Froala
const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY',
  heightMin: 300,
  placeholderText: 'Start typing',
  editorClass: 'my-editor',
  charCounterCount: true
});
```

[All options](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/options/)

## Plugins

In Lexical you import each package, register its nodes and its behavior. In Froala every loaded plugin is on; `pluginsEnabled` keeps only the plugins it names, and `pluginsDisabled` turns off the ones it names.

| Lexical package | Froala plugin or feature |
| --- | --- |
| `@lexical/rich-text` | Built in; headings with Paragraph Format, quotes with Quote |
| `@lexical/list` | Lists, `lists` |
| `@lexical/link` | Link, `link` |
| `@lexical/table` | Table, `table` |
| `@lexical/history` | Built in, with the `undo` and `redo` buttons |
| `@lexical/markdown` | Markdown, `markdown` |
| `@lexical/html` | Not needed; `html.get()` and `html.set()` |

```js
// Lexical
import { ListNode, ListItemNode, registerList } from '@lexical/list';
import { LinkNode } from '@lexical/link';

const editor = createEditor({ namespace: 'MyEditor', nodes: [ListNode, ListItemNode, LinkNode], onError });
registerRichText(editor);
registerList(editor);

// Froala, only these plugins
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  pluginsEnabled: ['align', 'lists', 'link', 'image', 'table']
});

// Froala, every plugin but these
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  pluginsDisabled: ['video', 'emoticons']
});
```

[Plugins](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/plugins/)

## Getting and Setting Content

Lexical turns its state into HTML with `@lexical/html`, inside `editor.read()` or `editor.update()`. Froala's content already is HTML.

### Reading

```js
// Lexical
import { $generateHtmlFromNodes } from '@lexical/html';

const html = editor.read(() => $generateHtmlFromNodes(editor, null));

// Froala
const html = editor.html.get();
```

### Writing

```js
// Lexical
import { $generateNodesFromDOM } from '@lexical/html';
import { $getRoot, $insertNodes } from 'lexical';

editor.update(() => {
  const dom = new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html');
  const nodes = $generateNodesFromDOM(editor, dom);
  $getRoot().clear();
  $getRoot().select();
  $insertNodes(nodes);
});

// Froala
editor.html.set('<p>Hello <strong>Froala</strong></p>');
editor.html.insert('<span>inserted</span>'); // at the cursor
```

If you store the serialized editor state as JSON, load each document into Lexical once and save the HTML from `$generateHtmlFromNodes`.

## Events

Lexical calls each update listener with the new editor state, and `registerUpdateListener` returns a function that removes it.

Froala takes handlers in the `events` option, or adds them later with `events.on()`. Inside a handler, `this` is the editor, so write a regular function rather than an arrow function. Froala has no method to remove a handler, so check a flag inside it instead.

```js
// Lexical
const removeListener = editor.registerUpdateListener(({ editorState }) => {
  editorState.read(() => console.log($generateHtmlFromNodes(editor, null)));
});
removeListener();

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  events: {
    initialized: function () {
      console.log('Editor ready');
    },
    contentChanged: function () {
      console.log(this.html.get());
    }
  }
});
```

[All events](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/events/)

## Methods

Lexical's methods sit on the editor; Froala groups them by module, such as `html`, `edit` and `events`.

```js
// Lexical
editor.setEditable(false);   // read-only
editor.setEditable(true);
editor.isEditable();
editor.focus();
editor.blur();
editor.setRootElement(null); // then call your cleanup functions

// Froala
editor.edit.off();           // read-only
editor.edit.on();
editor.edit.isDisabled();    // true when read-only
editor.events.focus();
editor.el.blur();            // no blur method; editor.el is the editable element
editor.destroy();
```

[All methods](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/methods/)

## Image Upload

Lexical's published packages have no image node and no upload; you write a node and a command and upload the file yourself. Froala uploads each image to `imageUploadURL` and inserts it from the link your server returns.

```js
// Lexical
import { createCommand, COMMAND_PRIORITY_EDITOR } from 'lexical';

export const INSERT_IMAGE_COMMAND = createCommand('INSERT_IMAGE');

editor.registerCommand(INSERT_IMAGE_COMMAND, (payload) => {
  // Upload payload.file, then insert your own ImageNode.
  return true;
}, COMMAND_PRIORITY_EDITOR);

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  imageUploadURL: '/upload_image',
  imageUploadParam: 'file',
  imageMaxSize: 5 * 1024 * 1024,
  imageAllowedTypes: ['jpeg', 'jpg', 'png'],
  events: {
    'image.uploaded': function (response) {
      // The server answered; the image is inserted next.
    },
    'image.error': function (error, response) {
      console.error(error.code, error.message);
    }
  }
});
```

The server saves the file and answers with JSON that holds its link, `{ "link": "https://example.com/image.jpg" }`.

- [Image upload](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/concepts/image/upload/)
- [Server SDKs](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/sdks/)

## React

Lexical builds a React editor from `LexicalComposer` and plugin components. Froala's wrapper is one component, `FroalaEditorComponent`, bound to your state through `model` and `onModelChange`.

```shell
npm install froala-editor react-froala-wysiwyg
```

```jsx
// Lexical
import { LexicalComposer } from '@lexical/react/LexicalComposer';
import { RichTextPlugin } from '@lexical/react/LexicalRichTextPlugin';
import { ContentEditable } from '@lexical/react/LexicalContentEditable';
import { HistoryPlugin } from '@lexical/react/LexicalHistoryPlugin';
import { OnChangePlugin } from '@lexical/react/LexicalOnChangePlugin';
import { LexicalErrorBoundary } from '@lexical/react/LexicalErrorBoundary';

const initialConfig = { namespace: 'MyEditor', onError: (e) => console.error(e) };

export default function Editor() {
  return (
    <LexicalComposer initialConfig={initialConfig}>
      <RichTextPlugin contentEditable={<ContentEditable />} ErrorBoundary={LexicalErrorBoundary} />
      <HistoryPlugin />
      <OnChangePlugin onChange={(editorState) => { /* save */ }} />
    </LexicalComposer>
  );
}
```

```jsx
// Froala
import { useState } from 'react';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_style.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins.pkgd.min.js';
import FroalaEditorComponent from 'react-froala-wysiwyg';

const config = { key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY', heightMin: 300 };

export default function Editor() {
  const [model, setModel] = useState('<p>Hello Froala</p>');
  return (
    <FroalaEditorComponent tag="textarea" config={config} model={model} onModelChange={setModel} />
  );
}
```

