# Migrate from Tiptap

Replace Tiptap with Froala in an existing project. Each section maps a Tiptap API to its Froala equivalent, with both in one code block.

Froala takes your license key as the `key` option. [Start a free trial](https://froala.com/wysiwyg_editor-download/) or [buy a license](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/pricing/) to get one. For help along the way, [contact support](https://froala.com/contact/?department=Tech%20Support).

## How the Editors Differ

Tiptap is a headless editor built on ProseMirror. It keeps content as a document tree, ships no interface, and you add each feature as an extension and build your own toolbar.

Froala works on HTML and draws its own toolbar, popups and dialogs. Its packaged file comes with its plugins loaded and on, so you choose what to show and set options rather than assemble the editor.

| Concept | Tiptap | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Create | `new Editor({ element, extensions })` | `new FroalaEditor('#editor', options)` |
| Target | A DOM element in `element` | A CSS selector or a DOM element |
| Features | Extensions in `extensions` | Plugins, narrowed with `pluginsEnabled` |
| Toolbar | None, you build it | `toolbarButtons` |
| Read, write | `getHTML()`, `commands.setContent()` | `html.get()`, `html.set()` |
| Events | `onUpdate`, `onCreate` and the like | `events: { contentChanged, initialized }` |
| Teardown | `destroy()` | `destroy()` |

Tiptap's core is open source under the MIT license; collaboration, document history, AI and some Pro extensions need a Tiptap subscription. Froala is commercial and takes a license key in its `key` option.

To keep the toolbar you built, Froala also has a headless mode, `headless: true`, which draws no toolbar or popups and leaves the editing to your controls. In the current release it covers a limited set of features. See [Headless Editor](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/concepts/custom/headless-editor/).

## Replace Tiptap

### Remove Tiptap

Uninstall the Tiptap packages you use, then delete their imports and the `new Editor()` or `useEditor()` setup.

```shell
npm uninstall @tiptap/core @tiptap/react @tiptap/pm @tiptap/starter-kit @tiptap/extension-image
```

### Add Froala

Install the package, or load the packaged files from the CDN. Both hold the editor and every plugin except Track Changes and Trim Video.

```shell
npm install froala-editor
```

```html
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/froala_editor.pkgd.min.js"></script>
```

### Start the Editor

Start Froala on the same element. What the element holds becomes the starting content. The editor's methods are ready when the function in the third argument runs, or the `initialized` event fires.

```js
// Tiptap
import { Editor } from '@tiptap/core';
import StarterKit from '@tiptap/starter-kit';

const editor = new Editor({
  element: document.querySelector('#editor'),
  extensions: [StarterKit],
  content: '<p>Hello World</p>'
});

// Froala
import FroalaEditor from 'froala-editor';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins.pkgd.min.js';

const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', { key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY' }, function () {
  this.html.set('<p>Hello World</p>');
});
```

## Configuration and Options

Tiptap configures each extension and sets editor attributes in `editorProps`. Froala takes every option in one object.

```js
// Tiptap
const editor = new Editor({
  element: document.querySelector('#editor'),
  extensions: [
    StarterKit.configure({ heading: { levels: [1, 2, 3] } })
  ],
  editable: true,
  editorProps: {
    attributes: { class: 'prose' }
  }
});

// Froala
const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  heightMin: 200,
  heightMax: 400,
  placeholderText: 'Start typing',
  editorClass: 'prose',
  paragraphFormat: { N: 'Normal', H1: 'Heading 1', H2: 'Heading 2', H3: 'Heading 3' }
});
```

`editorClass` puts the class on the editor's box rather than on the editable element.

[Options](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/options/)

## Plugins

Tiptap adds features as extensions. Froala's plugins are already loaded; `pluginsEnabled` keeps only the ones it names, and `pluginsDisabled` turns off the ones it names. A plugin in both lists stays off.

```js
// Tiptap
import StarterKit from '@tiptap/starter-kit';
import Image from '@tiptap/extension-image';
import TextAlign from '@tiptap/extension-text-align';

const editor = new Editor({
  element: document.querySelector('#editor'),
  extensions: [
    StarterKit.configure({ undoRedo: false }),
    Image,
    TextAlign.configure({ types: ['heading', 'paragraph'] })
  ]
});

// Froala, only the plugins you name
const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  pluginsEnabled: ['align', 'image', 'link', 'lists', 'table']
});

// Or every plugin but a few
const other = new FroalaEditor('#other', {
  pluginsDisabled: ['video', 'emoticons']
});
```

[Plugins](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/plugins/)

## Getting and Setting Content

Both read and write HTML. Tiptap can also give its document as JSON; Froala works with HTML only.

```js
// Tiptap
const html = editor.getHTML();
const json = editor.getJSON();
editor.commands.setContent('<p>New content</p>');
editor.commands.insertContent('<strong>inline</strong>');

// Froala
const html = editor.html.get();
editor.html.set('<p>New content</p>');
editor.html.insert('<strong>inline</strong>');
```

If you saved Tiptap JSON, convert it to HTML once with Tiptap's `generateHTML(json, extensions)`, from `@tiptap/core` in the browser or `@tiptap/html` on a server, before you load it into Froala.

## Events

Tiptap takes callbacks at the top of its options. Froala takes them in an `events` object, where `this` is the editor. Both can bind a handler later.

```js
// Tiptap
const editor = new Editor({
  element: document.querySelector('#editor'),
  extensions: [StarterKit],
  onCreate({ editor }) { console.log('Ready'); },
  onUpdate({ editor }) { console.log(editor.getHTML()); },
  onFocus({ editor }) {},
  onBlur({ editor }) {}
});
editor.on('update', () => console.log('Changed'));

// Froala
const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  events: {
    initialized: function () { console.log('Ready'); },
    contentChanged: function () { console.log(this.html.get()); },
    focus: function () {},
    blur: function () {}
  }
}, function () {
  this.events.on('contentChanged', function () { console.log('Changed'); });
});
```

[Events](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/events/)

## Methods

Tiptap chains commands. Froala calls methods grouped by module, such as `commands`, `edit` and `format`.

| To | Tiptap | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bold the selection | `chain().focus().toggleBold().run()` | `commands.bold()` |
| Read-only on, off | `setEditable(false)`, `setEditable(true)` | `edit.off()`, `edit.on()` |
| Is it editable | `isEditable` | `!edit.isDisabled()` |
| Focus | `commands.focus()` | `events.focus()` |
| Blur | `commands.blur()` | `el.blur()`, on the editable element |
| Is the selection bold | `isActive('bold')` | `format.is('strong')` |
| Teardown | `destroy()` | `destroy()` |

```js
// Tiptap
editor.chain().focus().toggleBold().run();
editor.setEditable(false);
editor.isActive('bold');

// Froala
editor.commands.bold();
editor.edit.off();
editor.format.is('strong');
```

`format.is()` takes a tag name, so bold is `'strong'` and italic `'em'`. `events.disableBlur()` stops the blur and focus events; it doesn't move focus.

[Methods](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/methods/)

## Image Upload

Tiptap's Image extension shows an image node; you write the upload and insert the URL. Froala's Image plugin uploads the file itself. It sends each image to `imageUploadURL` as a `POST` form, in the field `imageUploadParam` names (`file` by default), and checks the size and type first.

```js
// Tiptap
import Image from '@tiptap/extension-image';

const editor = new Editor({
  element: document.querySelector('#editor'),
  extensions: [StarterKit, Image]
});

async function uploadAndInsert(file) {
  const body = new FormData();
  body.append('file', file);
  const res = await fetch('/upload_image', { method: 'POST', body });
  const { link } = await res.json();
  editor.chain().focus().setImage({ src: link }).run();
}

// Froala
const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  imageUploadURL: '/upload_image',
  imageUploadParam: 'file',
  imageMaxSize: 5 * 1024 * 1024,
  imageAllowedTypes: ['jpeg', 'jpg', 'png'],
  events: {
    'image.uploaded': function (response) {
      console.log('Uploaded', response);
    },
    'image.error': function (error, response) {
      console.error(error.code, error.message);
    }
  }
});
```

Your server returns the image's address as `{ "link": "/path/to/image.jpg" }`.

[Image upload](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/concepts/image/upload/)

## React

Tiptap's React package gives you `useEditor` and `EditorContent`. `react-froala-wysiwyg` gives you one component that binds its content with `model` and `onModelChange`.

```shell
npm uninstall @tiptap/react @tiptap/pm @tiptap/starter-kit
npm install froala-editor react-froala-wysiwyg
```

```jsx
// Tiptap
import { useEditor, EditorContent } from '@tiptap/react';
import StarterKit from '@tiptap/starter-kit';

export function MyEditor() {
  const editor = useEditor({
    extensions: [StarterKit],
    content: '<p>Hello World</p>',
    immediatelyRender: false,
    onUpdate: ({ editor }) => console.log(editor.getHTML())
  });

  return <EditorContent editor={editor} />;
}

// Froala
import { useState } from 'react';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_style.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins.pkgd.min.js';
import FroalaEditorComponent from 'react-froala-wysiwyg';

const config = { key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY' };

export function MyEditor() {
  const [model, setModel] = useState('<p>Hello World</p>');

  return (
    <FroalaEditorComponent tag="textarea" config={config} model={model} onModelChange={setModel} />
  );
}
```

The [Angular](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/framework-plugins/angular/) and [Vue](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/framework-plugins/vue-js-3/) packages take the same options, with their own bindings for the content.

[React guide](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/framework-plugins/react/)

## Extension Lookup

Find the Froala plugin or option for each Tiptap extension you use.

| Feature | Tiptap | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bold, italic, underline | In StarterKit | Core, the `bold`, `italic` and `underline` buttons |
| Headings | `Heading`, in StarterKit | The `paragraphFormat` plugin and option |
| Lists | `BulletList`, `OrderedList`, in StarterKit | The `lists` plugin, `formatUL` and `formatOL` |
| Links | `Link`, in StarterKit | The `link` plugin, `insertLink` |
| Images | `@tiptap/extension-image`, no upload | The `image` plugin, with upload |
| Tables | `@tiptap/extension-table` | The `table` plugin |
| Text alignment | `@tiptap/extension-text-align` | The `align` plugin |
| Code blocks | `CodeBlock`, in StarterKit | The `codeSnippet` plugin, or `PRE` in `paragraphFormat` |
| Placeholder | `Placeholder`, from `@tiptap/extensions` | The `placeholderText` option |
| Character count | `CharacterCount`, from `@tiptap/extensions` | The `charCounter` and `wordCounter` plugins |
| Undo, redo | `UndoRedo`, in StarterKit | Core, the `undo` and `redo` buttons |
| Markdown | `@tiptap/markdown` | The `markdown` plugin |
| Toolbar | None, you build it | `toolbarButtons` |

