# Migrate from Quill

Move an editor from Quill to Froala. Each section pairs a Quill call with its Froala counterpart, checked against Quill 2.0.3, the current release.

## Before You Start

Quill keeps the content as a Delta, a JSON list of operations, and renders HTML from it. Froala keeps the content as HTML. Stored HTML loads into Froala as it is. Stored Deltas need one conversion to HTML, shown in [Getting and Setting Content](#getting-and-setting-content).

| Concept | Quill | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Start | `new Quill('#editor', options)` | `new FroalaEditor('#editor', options)` |
| Features | `modules` | Plugins, all on once loaded |
| Toolbar | `modules.toolbar`, format names | `toolbarButtons`, button names |
| Read | `getSemanticHTML()`, `getContents()` | `html.get()` |
| Write | `setContents(delta)`, `clipboard.dangerouslyPasteHTML(html)` | `html.set(html)` |
| Events | `quill.on('text-change', handler)` | The `events` option, or `events.on()` |
| Tear down | No destroy method | `destroy()` |
| License | BSD-3-Clause, free | Commercial, a license key in the `key` option |

Without a valid key, Froala shows a small notice, and every feature keeps working. Use the key from your [license](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/pricing/) or a [free trial](https://froala.com/wysiwyg_editor-download/).

## Replace Quill

### Remove Quill

Remove the Quill stylesheet, script and start call. Keep the container element; Froala starts on the same one.

```html
<!-- Remove -->
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/quill@2.0.3/dist/quill.snow.css" rel="stylesheet">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/quill@2.0.3/dist/quill.js"></script>
```

With npm, remove the package, and the React wrapper if you use one.

```shell
npm uninstall quill
npm uninstall react-quill react-quill-new   # if you use a React wrapper
```

### Add Froala

#### From a CDN

```html
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/froala_editor.pkgd.min.js"></script>
```

`froala_editor.pkgd.min.js` holds the editor and every plugin except Track Changes and Trim Video.

#### From npm

```shell
npm install froala-editor
```

```js
import FroalaEditor from 'froala-editor';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins.pkgd.min.js';
```

[Installation](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/overview/)

### Start the Editor

Both take a selector or an element, and both start with the element's HTML as their content.

```js
// Quill
const quill = new Quill('#editor', { theme: 'snow' });

// Froala
const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', { key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY' });
```

#### Other Elements

Froala also edits an image, a button or a link in place, and with `initOnClick` it starts only the minimum on page load and the rest on the first click.

```js
new FroalaEditor('#editor', { initOnClick: true });

new FroalaEditor('img#photo');
```

[Init on image example](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/examples/init-on-image/)

## Configuration and Options

Both take an options object as the second argument. Quill nests features under `modules`; Froala's options are all top-level keys.

### Common Options

| Quill | Froala |
| --- | --- |
| `theme: 'snow'` | The default toolbar, no option needed |
| `theme: 'bubble'` | `toolbarInline: true` |
| `placeholder` | `placeholderText` |
| `readOnly: true` | `this.edit.off()` in the `initialized` event |
| `modules.toolbar` | `toolbarButtons` |
| `formats` | `htmlAllowedTags` and `htmlAllowedAttrs` |

```js
// Quill
const quill = new Quill('#editor', {
  theme: 'snow',
  placeholder: 'Compose an epic...',
  readOnly: true,
  modules: {
    toolbar: [['bold', 'italic'], ['link', 'image']]
  }
});

// Froala
const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  placeholderText: 'Compose an epic...',
  toolbarButtons: [['bold', 'italic'], ['insertLink', 'insertImage']],
  events: {
    initialized: function () {
      this.edit.off(); // read-only
    }
  }
});
```

[All options](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/options/)

### Building the Toolbar

Quill's toolbar lists formats; Froala's lists buttons. Each inner list is a group of buttons. `toolbarButtonsMD`, `toolbarButtonsSM` and `toolbarButtonsXS` set the toolbar for smaller screens.

| Quill format | Froala button |
| --- | --- |
| `bold`, `italic`, `underline` | `bold`, `italic`, `underline` |
| `strike` | `strikeThrough` |
| `{ script: 'sub' }`, `{ script: 'super' }` | `subscript`, `superscript` |
| `{ header: [] }` | `paragraphFormat` |
| `{ font: [] }`, `{ size: [] }` | `fontFamily`, `fontSize` |
| `{ color: [] }`, `{ background: [] }` | `textColor`, `backgroundColor` |
| `blockquote` | `quote` |
| `code-block` | `codeSnippet` |
| `{ list: 'ordered' }`, `{ list: 'bullet' }` | `formatOL`, `formatUL` |
| `{ indent: '-1' }`, `{ indent: '+1' }` | `outdent`, `indent` |
| `{ align: [] }` | `align` |
| `link`, `image`, `video` | `insertLink`, `insertImage`, `insertVideo` |
| `clean` | `clearFormatting` |

```js
// Quill
new Quill('#editor', {
  theme: 'snow',
  modules: {
    toolbar: [
      ['bold', 'italic', 'underline', 'strike'],
      ['blockquote', 'code-block'],
      [{ list: 'ordered' }, { list: 'bullet' }],
      [{ align: [] }],
      ['clean']
    ]
  }
});

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  toolbarButtons: [
    ['bold', 'italic', 'underline', 'strikeThrough'],
    ['codeSnippet'],
    ['align', 'formatUL', 'formatOL', 'quote', 'clearFormatting']
  ]
});
```

The button that shows and edits the HTML source is `html`.

Quill's syntax module needs highlight.js on the page.

Froala's Code Snippet plugin needs Prism.js on the page.

## Plugins

Quill turns modules on in `modules`. In Froala every loaded plugin is on; `pluginsEnabled` keeps only the plugins it names, and `pluginsDisabled` turns off the ones it names. Without the packaged file, load each plugin's script and stylesheet.

| Quill module | Froala |
| --- | --- |
| `toolbar` | `toolbarButtons` |
| `history` | Built in, with the `undo` and `redo` buttons |
| `syntax` | The Code Snippet plugin, `codeSnippet` |
| `keyboard` | Built-in shortcuts, `shortcutsEnabled` |
| `uploader` | The Image plugin's upload options |

```js
// Quill
new Quill('#editor', {
  theme: 'snow',
  modules: {
    history: { delay: 1000 },
    toolbar: [['bold', 'italic'], ['link', 'image']]
  }
});

// Froala, only these plugins
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  pluginsEnabled: ['image', 'link', 'table', 'codeView']
});

// Froala, every plugin but these
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  pluginsDisabled: ['video', 'fontFamily']
});
```

[Plugins](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/plugins/)

## Getting and Setting Content

### Reading

```js
// Quill
const html = quill.getSemanticHTML();
const delta = quill.getContents();
const text = quill.getText();

// Froala
const html = editor.html.get();
const text = editor.el.textContent; // editor.el is the editable element
```

### Writing

```js
// Quill
quill.clipboard.dangerouslyPasteHTML('<p>Hello <strong>World!</strong></p>');
quill.clipboard.dangerouslyPasteHTML(5, '<span>inserted</span>');

// Froala
editor.html.set('<p>Hello <strong>World!</strong></p>');
editor.html.insert('<span>inserted</span>'); // at the cursor
```

If you store Deltas, convert each one to HTML with Quill before the switch, then save the HTML.

```js
quill.setContents(storedDelta);
const html = quill.getSemanticHTML(); // save this, then load it with editor.html.set(html)
```

## Events

Quill adds listeners with `quill.on()`. Froala takes handlers in the `events` option, or adds them later with `events.on()`. Inside a handler, `this` is the editor, so write a regular function rather than an arrow function.

| Quill | Froala |
| --- | --- |
| `text-change` | `contentChanged` |
| `selection-change` with a range after `null` | `focus` |
| `selection-change` with a `null` range | `blur` |
| `selection-change` as the cursor moves | No single event; read `this.selection.get()` in `keyup` and `mouseup` |

### Content Changes

```js
// Quill
quill.on('text-change', (delta, oldDelta, source) => {
  if (source === 'user') console.log(quill.getSemanticHTML());
});

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  events: {
    contentChanged: function () {
      console.log(this.html.get());
    }
  }
});
```

### Adding Handlers Later

The function passed as the third argument runs once the editor is ready, with the editor as `this`. Froala has no method to remove a handler, so where Quill calls `off()`, check a flag inside the handler.

```js
// Quill
quill.on('text-change', handler);
quill.off('text-change', handler);

// Froala
let listening = true;
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {}, function () {
  this.events.on('contentChanged', function () {
    if (listening) console.log('changed');
  });
});
```

[All events](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/events/)

## Methods

Quill's methods sit on the instance; Froala groups them by module, such as `html`, `edit` and `events`.

### Read-Only Mode

```js
// Quill
quill.disable(); // or quill.enable(false)
quill.enable();

// Froala
editor.edit.off();
editor.edit.on();
```

### Focus, Blur and Tear Down

```js
// Quill
quill.focus();
quill.blur();
// No destroy method; remove the element and drop the reference.

// Froala
editor.events.focus();
editor.el.blur();   // no blur method; editor.el is the editable element
editor.destroy();   // returns the element to its state before the editor
```

[All methods](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/methods/)

## Image Upload

Quill inserts PNG and JPEG images as base64 data URLs unless you add your own handler. Froala uploads each image to `imageUploadURL` and inserts it from the link your server returns.

### Quill Upload Handler

```js
const toolbar = quill.getModule('toolbar');
toolbar.addHandler('image', () => {
  const input = document.createElement('input');
  input.type = 'file';
  input.onchange = async () => {
    const body = new FormData();
    body.append('file', input.files[0]);
    const res = await fetch('/upload_image', { method: 'POST', body });
    const { url } = await res.json();
    const range = quill.getSelection(true);
    quill.insertEmbed(range.index, 'image', url);
  };
  input.click();
});
```

### Froala Upload Options

```js
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  imageUploadURL: '/upload_image',
  imageUploadParam: 'file',
  imageMaxSize: 5 * 1024 * 1024,
  imageAllowedTypes: ['jpeg', 'jpg', 'png'],
  events: {
    'image.uploaded': function (response) {
      // The server answered; the image is inserted next.
    },
    'image.error': function (error, response) {
      console.error(error.code, error.message);
    }
  }
});
```

The server saves the file and answers with JSON that holds its link, `{ "link": "https://example.com/image.jpg" }`.

- [Image upload](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/concepts/image/upload/)
- [Server SDKs](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/sdks/)

## React

Quill has no React component of its own. The community `react-quill` package wraps Quill 1 (it depends on `quill ^1.3.7`); its fork `react-quill-new` wraps Quill 2. Froala's wrapper is `react-froala-wysiwyg`, installed with the editor.

```shell
npm install froala-editor react-froala-wysiwyg
```

```jsx
// Quill, with react-quill-new
import { useState } from 'react';
import ReactQuill from 'react-quill-new';
import 'react-quill-new/dist/quill.snow.css';

export default function Editor() {
  const [value, setValue] = useState('<p>Hello</p>');
  return <ReactQuill theme="snow" value={value} onChange={setValue} />;
}
```

```jsx
// Froala
import { useState } from 'react';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_style.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins.pkgd.min.js';
import FroalaEditorComponent from 'react-froala-wysiwyg';

const config = { placeholderText: 'Edit me' };

export default function Editor() {
  const [model, setModel] = useState('<p>Hello</p>');
  return (
    <FroalaEditorComponent tag="textarea" config={config} model={model} onModelChange={setModel} />
  );
}
```

The component works with server-side rendering. To add plugins in Next.js or another server-rendered app, load them in the browser first, as the [React guide](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/framework-plugins/react/#server-side-rendering) shows.

- [React guide](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/framework-plugins/react/)
- [Angular guide](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/framework-plugins/angular/)
- [Vue guide](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/framework-plugins/vue-js-3/)

