# Migrate from Summernote

Move an editor from Summernote to Froala. Each section pairs a Summernote call with its Froala counterpart, checked against Summernote 0.9.1, the current release.

## Before You Start

Summernote is a jQuery plugin. One call, `$(selector).summernote()`, starts the editor with an options object or runs a command named by a string, such as `'code'`. It needs jQuery, and its Bootstrap builds need Bootstrap; the Lite build doesn't.

Froala needs neither. You create an editor with `new FroalaEditor(selector, options)`, keep it, and call its methods, such as `editor.html.get()`. Both editors work in HTML, so stored content carries over as it is.

| Concept | Summernote | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Start | `$('#editor').summernote(options)` | `new FroalaEditor('#editor', options)` |
| Features | Built into each build, shown by toolbar buttons | Plugins, all on once loaded |
| Toolbar | `toolbar`, a list of `[group, [buttons]]` | `toolbarButtons`, a list of button groups |
| Read | `$('#editor').summernote('code')` | `editor.html.get()` |
| Write | `$('#editor').summernote('code', html)` | `editor.html.set(html)` |
| Events | `callbacks: { onChange }` | `events: { contentChanged }` |
| Tear down | `$('#editor').summernote('destroy')` | `editor.destroy()` |
| License | MIT, free | Commercial, a license key in the `key` option |

Without a valid key, Froala shows a small notice, and every feature keeps working. Use the key from your [license](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/pricing/) or a [free trial](https://froala.com/wysiwyg_editor-download/).

## Replace Summernote

### Remove Summernote

Remove the Summernote files, and jQuery and Bootstrap if nothing else on the page uses them. Keep the `div` or `textarea`; Froala starts on the same element.

```html
<!-- Remove -->
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/summernote@0.9.1/dist/summernote-bs4.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/summernote@0.9.1/dist/summernote-bs4.min.js"></script>
```

```shell
npm uninstall summernote
```

### Add Froala

```html
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/froala_editor.pkgd.min.js"></script>
```

Or install it with npm and import it.

```shell
npm install froala-editor
```

```js
import FroalaEditor from 'froala-editor';
import 'froala-editor/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css';
import 'froala-editor/js/plugins.pkgd.min.js';
```

The packaged files hold every plugin except Track Changes and Trim Video.

[Installation](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/overview/)

### Start the Editor

Keep the editor the constructor returns; it is how you call every method later. Both editors start with the element's HTML as their content. Run the constructor after the element is in the page, at the end of the body or in a `DOMContentLoaded` listener.

```js
// Summernote
$(document).ready(function () {
  $('#editor').summernote();
});

// Froala
const editor = new FroalaEditor('#editor', { key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY' });
```

## Configuration and Options

Both take a plain options object. The toolbar changes shape most. Summernote names each group, `['font', ['bold', 'underline']]`; in Froala each inner list is a group.

### Common Options

```js
// Summernote
$('#editor').summernote({
  placeholder: 'Write here...',
  height: 300,
  focus: true,
  tabSize: 2,
  lang: 'de-DE',
  toolbar: [
    ['style', ['style']],
    ['font', ['bold', 'italic', 'underline', 'clear']],
    ['para', ['ul', 'ol', 'paragraph']],
    ['insert', ['link', 'picture']]
  ]
});

// Froala, with js/languages/de.js loaded
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  key: 'YOUR_LICENSE_KEY',
  placeholderText: 'Write here...',
  height: 300,
  autofocus: true,
  tabSpaces: 2,
  language: 'de',
  toolbarButtons: [
    ['paragraphFormat'],
    ['bold', 'italic', 'underline'],
    ['insertLink', 'insertImage'],
    ['align', 'formatUL', 'formatOL', 'clearFormatting']
  ]
});
```

### Option Names

| Summernote | Froala | Note |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `placeholder` | `placeholderText` |  |
| `height` | `height` | `heightMin` and `heightMax` set a range instead |
| `focus` | `autofocus` |  |
| `tabSize`, the name the source reads, though Summernote's examples write `tabsize` | `tabSpaces` | Froala's default is 0, so Tab moves focus out of the editor |
| `lang` | `language` | Load the file from `js/languages`, such as `de.js`; English needs none |
| `spellCheck` | `spellcheck` | On by default in both |
| `airMode` | `toolbarInline: true` |  |
| `styleTags` | `paragraphFormat` | An object of tags and labels |
| `fontNames` | `fontFamily` | An object of font stacks and labels |
| `toolbar` | `toolbarButtons` | `toolbarButtonsMD`, `SM` and `XS` set smaller screens |

### Toolbar Buttons

| Summernote button | Froala button |
| --- | --- |
| `style` | `paragraphFormat` |
| `bold`, `italic`, `underline`, `strikethrough` | `bold`, `italic`, `underline`, `strikeThrough` |
| `clear` | `clearFormatting` |
| `fontname`, `fontsize` | `fontFamily`, `fontSize` |
| `color` | `textColor`, `backgroundColor` |
| `ul`, `ol` | `formatUL`, `formatOL` |
| `paragraph`, alignment and indent | `align`, `outdent`, `indent` |
| `table` | `insertTable` |
| `link`, `picture`, `video` | `insertLink`, `insertImage`, `insertVideo` |
| `fullscreen`, `codeview`, `help` | `fullscreen`, `html`, `help` |

[All options](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/options/)

## Plugins

Summernote builds its features into each build and shows them through toolbar buttons. In Froala every loaded plugin is on; `pluginsEnabled` keeps only the plugins it names, and `pluginsDisabled` turns off the ones it names. A plugin in both lists stays off.

```js
// Summernote
$('#editor').summernote({
  toolbar: [['insert', ['link', 'picture', 'video', 'table']]]
});

// Froala, only these plugins
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  pluginsEnabled: ['link', 'image', 'video', 'table', 'lists']
});

// Froala, every plugin but these
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  pluginsDisabled: ['video', 'table']
});
```

[Plugins](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/plugins/)

## Getting and Setting Content

Summernote's `'code'` command reads the HTML with no argument and writes it with one. Froala has a method for each, and the HTML you read from Summernote goes straight into Froala.

### Reading

```js
// Summernote
const markup = $('#editor').summernote('code');

// Froala
const markup = editor.html.get();
```

### Writing

```js
// Summernote
$('#editor').summernote('code', '<p>Hello world</p>');
$('#editor').summernote('pasteHTML', '<strong>inline</strong>');

// Froala
editor.html.set('<p>Hello world</p>');
editor.html.insert('<strong>inline</strong>'); // at the cursor
```

`html.insert()` takes HTML, so where Summernote calls `insertText`, escape `<` and `&` in the text first.

## Events

Summernote takes handlers in `callbacks`; Froala takes them in `events`, or adds them later with `events.on()`. Inside a Froala handler, `this` is the editor, so write a regular function rather than an arrow function.

### Handlers at Start

```js
// Summernote
$('#editor').summernote({
  callbacks: {
    onInit: function () {
      console.log('Editor ready');
    },
    onChange: function (contents) {
      console.log(contents);
    }
  }
});

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  events: {
    initialized: function () {
      console.log('Editor ready');
    },
    contentChanged: function () {
      console.log(this.html.get());
    }
  }
});
```

### Event Names

| When | Summernote | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Ready | `onInit` | `initialized` |
| Content changed | `onChange` | `contentChanged` |
| Focus | `onFocus` | `focus` |
| Blur | `onBlur` | `blur` |
| Key down, key up | `onKeydown`, `onKeyup` | `keydown`, `keyup` |
| Paste | `onPaste` | `paste.before`, `paste.after` |
| Image chosen | `onImageUpload` | `image.beforeUpload` |

[All events](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/events/)

## Methods

Summernote runs a method by its name, `$('#editor').summernote('disable')`. Froala calls it on the editor you kept, `editor.edit.off()`.

### Common Methods

| Action | Summernote | Froala |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Disable, enable | `'disable'`, `'enable'` | `edit.off()`, `edit.on()` |
| Focus | `'focus'` | `events.focus()` |
| Is empty | `'isEmpty'` | `core.isEmpty()` |
| Undo, redo | `'undo'`, `'redo'` | `commands.undo()`, `commands.redo()` |
| Clear | `'reset'` | `html.set('')` |
| Code view | `'codeview.toggle'` | `codeView.toggle()` |
| Destroy | `'destroy'` | `destroy()` |

### Enable, Disable and Tear Down

```js
// Summernote
$('#editor').summernote('disable');
$('#editor').summernote('enable');
$('#editor').summernote('destroy');

// Froala
editor.edit.off();
editor.edit.on();
editor.destroy();
```

[All methods](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/methods/)

## Image Upload

Summernote inserts images as base64 data URLs unless `onImageUpload` posts the file to your server. Froala uploads each image to `imageUploadURL` and inserts it from the link your server returns, with progress and error events.

```js
// Summernote
$('#editor').summernote({
  callbacks: {
    onImageUpload: function (files) {
      const data = new FormData();
      data.append('file', files[0]);
      $.ajax({
        url: '/upload',
        method: 'POST',
        data: data,
        processData: false,
        contentType: false,
        success: function (url) {
          $('#editor').summernote('insertImage', url);
        }
      });
    }
  }
});

// Froala
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  imageUploadURL: '/upload',
  imageUploadParam: 'file',
  events: {
    'image.uploaded': function (response) {
      console.log('Uploaded', response);
    },
    'image.error': function (error, response) {
      console.error(error.message);
    }
  }
});
```

The server saves the file and answers with JSON that holds its link, `{ "link": "/uploads/photo.jpg" }`.

