# .NET Image Resize

Resize images on the server as they are uploaded, with the `ResizeGeometry` option of `FroalaEditor.ImageOptions`.

## How It Works

1. The editor uploads the image to your server.
2. The SDK resizes the image as it saves it.

## Image Upload

Set up the upload first, as in [Image Server Upload](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/sdks/dotnet/image-server-upload/). Resizing an image in the editor only changes the size it shows at. The file keeps its size until the server resizes it.

## Resize Image

Give `ImageOptions` a `MagickGeometry`. The SDK reads the upload with Magick.NET, calls `Resize` with your geometry and writes the result to disk.

```csharp
using ImageMagick;

// Fit the image inside 300 by 300 pixels.
MagickGeometry resizeGeometry = new MagickGeometry(300, 300);

// Or make it exactly 300 by 300, whatever its proportions.
resizeGeometry.IgnoreAspectRatio = true;

FroalaEditor.ImageOptions options = new FroalaEditor.ImageOptions
{
    ResizeGeometry = resizeGeometry
};

object response = FroalaEditor.Image.Upload(HttpContext, "wwwroot/uploads/", options);
```

A geometry fits the image inside the size and keeps its proportions, unless `IgnoreAspectRatio` is on. Every other `MagickGeometry` setting works too. See the [Magick.NET resize guide](https://github.com/dlemstra/Magick.NET/blob/main/docs/ResizeImage.md).

## Complete Example

```js
new FroalaEditor('#editor', {
  imageUploadURL: '/FroalaApi/UploadImageResize',

  imageUploadParams: {
    id: 'my_editor'
  }
});
```

