The server should listen for any delete request and process it accordingly. The initialization step makes the image path available in the `javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest` parameter. The `com.froala.editor.Image.delete` method from the Java SDK expects the path of the image to remove from disk.

```java
String src = request.getParameter("src");
Image.delete(request, src);
```

`Image.delete` removes whatever path it gets, and the request comes from the browser. Check that `src` points inside your image folder before you pass it on.

