# Node.js SDK

`wysiwyg-editor-node-sdk` is the server side of the editor for Node.js. It stores the images and files users insert, signs uploads to Amazon S3, and runs the backend for real-time collaboration. Its source is on [GitHub](https://github.com/froala/wysiwyg-editor-node-sdk).

## Overview

One package holds every module. Use only the ones you need, each from your own routes.

### File and Image Handling

| Module | What it does | Guide |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Image` | Stores uploaded images on your server, resizes and validates them, deletes them and lists them for the image manager. | [Image Server Upload](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/sdks/nodejs/image-server-upload/) |
| `File` | Stores and validates uploaded files, and deletes them. | [File Server Upload](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/sdks/nodejs/file-server-upload/) |
| `Video` | Stores and deletes uploaded MP4, WebM and Ogg videos, the same way as `Image`. | [Image Reference](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/sdks/nodejs/references/image/) |
| `S3` | Signs uploads, so the editor sends images and files straight to an Amazon S3 bucket. | [Image S3 Upload](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/sdks/nodejs/image-s3-upload/) |

### Real-Time Collaboration Backend

| Module | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `Collaborative` | A WebSocket relay. It groups clients by document and passes each edit to the others. The editor's Collaborative plugin does the syncing, with Yjs. |
| `CollabPersistence` | REST routes that store suggestions and comments, with their replies and status. |
| `VersionControl` | REST routes that store named and automatic snapshots of a document and list its history. |
| `AsyncSave` | REST routes that save and load a document's latest content when people edit it without real-time sync. |

The three storage modules keep their data in SQLite through `better-sqlite3`, which installs with the SDK, and can share one database file. One HTTP server runs the whole backend.

[Collaboration Overview](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/sdks/nodejs/collaboration-overview/)

## Requirements

| Needs | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Node.js 22 or later | The SDK sets no Node.js version itself. Its `better-sqlite3` dependency needs Node.js 20 or later. Node.js 20 is out of support since April 2026, so use a release that still gets updates. |
| ImageMagick | The README lists it as a prerequisite. The SDK calls it to resize images. |
| Express | The collaboration storage modules add their routes to an Express app. Uploads read the plain Node.js request and the other methods take paths, so they work with any framework. |

The SDK is released with each editor release, most recently on 30 September 2026. Its upload, resize and S3 code dates from 2016, with one small change to the image module in 2022.

It resizes images with `gm`, whose author stopped maintaining it in February 2025.

## Install the SDK

Install it from npm with Express, which the examples use.

```shell
npm install wysiwyg-editor-node-sdk express
```

## Import the SDK in Your App

The package is a CommonJS module. Each module is a property of what it exports.

```js
const FroalaEditor = require('wysiwyg-editor-node-sdk');

// FroalaEditor.Image, FroalaEditor.File, FroalaEditor.Video, FroalaEditor.S3,
// FroalaEditor.Collaborative, FroalaEditor.CollabPersistence,
// FroalaEditor.VersionControl and FroalaEditor.AsyncSave
```

### Example

A `server.js` with every route the guides use, from the SDK's own example. The routes have no authentication, so add your own before you put it online.

```js
const http = require('http');
const path = require('path');
const fs = require('fs');
const express = require('express');
const FroalaEditor = require('wysiwyg-editor-node-sdk');

const { Image, File, S3, Collaborative, CollabPersistence, VersionControl, AsyncSave } = FroalaEditor;

const app = express();
app.use(express.json({ limit: '5mb' }));
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: false, limit: '5mb' }));

// The SDK saves uploads relative to the folder of the app's main file.
fs.mkdirSync(path.join(__dirname, 'uploads'), { recursive: true });
app.use('/uploads', express.static(path.join(__dirname, 'uploads')));

// Send the SDK's result to the editor, or an error status it reports.
function reply(res) {
  return function (err, data) {
    if (err) {
      return res.status(400).json({ error: String(err) });
    }
    res.json(data || {});
  };
}

// Delete only what is inside the uploads folder.
function uploaded(src) {
  return typeof src === 'string' && src.startsWith('/uploads/') && !src.includes('..');
}

app.post('/upload_image', function (req, res) {
  Image.upload(req, '/uploads/', reply(res));
});

app.post('/upload_image_resize', function (req, res) {
  Image.upload(req, '/uploads/', { resize: [300, 300] }, reply(res));
});

app.post('/upload_file', function (req, res) {
  File.upload(req, '/uploads/', reply(res));
});

app.post('/delete_image', function (req, res) {
  if (!uploaded(req.body.src)) return res.status(400).end();
  Image.delete(req.body.src, reply(res));
});

app.post('/delete_file', function (req, res) {
  if (!uploaded(req.body.src)) return res.status(400).end();
  File.delete(req.body.src, reply(res));
});

app.get('/load_images', function (req, res) {
  Image.list('/uploads/', reply(res));
});

app.get('/get_signature', function (req, res) {
  res.json(S3.getHash({
    bucket: process.env.AWS_BUCKET,
    region: process.env.AWS_REGION,
    keyStart: 'uploads/',
    acl: 'public-read',
    accessKey: process.env.AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID,
    secretKey: process.env.AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
  }));
});

// Collaboration: suggestions, comments, versions and saved content in one SQLite file.
const dbPath = path.join(__dirname, 'collab.db');
CollabPersistence.attachRoutes(app, { dbPath });
VersionControl.attachRoutes(app, { dbPath });
AsyncSave.attachRoutes(app, { dbPath });

app.get('/health', function (req, res) {
  res.json(Collaborative.getStats());
});

// One HTTP server for the routes and the WebSocket relay.
const server = http.createServer(app);
Collaborative.attachToServer(server);
server.listen(3000);
```

