# Node.js File Server Delete

## How it works

1. Code intercepts the file removed from the editor.
2. Removing a file sends to the server a request to delete the file from disk.
3. Once the request reaches the server, it deletes the file.

[Jump to Complete Example](#complete-example)

## Intercept file being removed

Removing a file from the editor triggers the [`file.unlink`](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/events/#file.unlink) event, with the removed link. It fires once the link is gone from the editable area, so you can use it to delete the file from the server.

## Send request to the server

There is no built-in feature that makes the request to the server, however you can use an AJAX request.

```html
<script>
  new FroalaEditor('.selector', {
    events: {
      // Catch the file being removed.
      'file.unlink': function (link) {
        fetch('/delete_file', {
          // Request method.
          method: 'POST',

          // Request params.
          body: new URLSearchParams({ src: link.getAttribute('href') })
        })
        .then(function (response) {
          console.log(response.ok ? 'File was deleted' : 'File delete problem');
        });
      }
    }
  });
</script>
```

## Delete the file

The server implementation is responsible for receiving the request and handling it appropriately. The code on the previous step makes the file path available in the body of the request, as `request.body.src`. The `FroalaEditor.File.delete()` method from the Node.JS SDK expects the path of the file to remove from disk.

The path of the file is relative to the folder of your app's main file. The SDK deletes whatever path it gets, so check that it is inside your uploads folder first, as the example below does.

```js
FroalaEditor.File.delete(req.body.src, function(err) { ... });
```

## Complete Example

```html
<script>
  new FroalaEditor('.selector', {
    events: {
      // Catch the file being removed.
      'file.unlink': function (link) {
        fetch('/delete_file', {
          // Request method.
          method: 'POST',

          // Request params.
          body: new URLSearchParams({ src: link.getAttribute('href') })
        })
        .then(function (response) {
          console.log(response.ok ? 'File was deleted' : 'File delete problem');
        });
      }
    }
  });
</script>
```

```js
const express = require('express');
const FroalaEditor = require('wysiwyg-editor-node-sdk');

const app = express();

// Read form posts into req.body.
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: false }));

// Listen to the delete request.
app.post('/delete_file', function (req, res) {
  const src = req.body.src;

  // Delete only what is inside the uploads folder.
  if (typeof src !== 'string' || !src.startsWith('/uploads/') || src.includes('..')) {
    return res.status(400).end();
  }

  // Do delete.
  FroalaEditor.File.delete(src, function(err) {
    if (err) {
      return res.status(404).end(JSON.stringify(err));
    }

    return res.end();
  });
});

app.listen(3000);
```

