# Headless Mode Example: Build Your Own Editor Toolbar

This live example shows Froala’s headless mode in action. Froala keeps the editing engine and hands the interface to you: every button in the toolbar below is your own HTML, and each one calls a single Froala [API method](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/methods/). Try it, then copy the code or open it in JSFiddle.

## Headless Mode

NEW IN 5.5

Set the `headless` option to `true` and Froala renders a clean editable area. The built-in toolbar, popups and default editor styling step aside, so your app's own design system shapes the whole experience.

